NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENSE
---------------------------
This repository does not redistribute ChaosNLI. The premises, hypotheses, observations and the
100-annotator label distributions live in the ChaosNLI release, which is licensed
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 (CC BY-NC 4.0):

  Nie, Y., Zhou, X., & Bansal, M. (2020). What Can We Learn from Collective Human Opinions on
  Natural Language Inference Data? EMNLP 2020. https://github.com/easonnie/chaos_nli

Joining our votes with ChaosNLI (see `scripts/join_chaosnli.py`) produces a derived dataset that
is subject to ChaosNLI's non-commercial terms. The item ids in `items/` are reproduced from
ChaosNLI under attribution as a bare index, so that our votes can be aligned with it.

The code under `scripts/` is licensed separately under the MIT License; see LICENSE-CODE.
